{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01149",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.26,
      "end_seconds": 5.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "uh, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.62,
      "end_seconds": 10.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.12,
      "end_seconds": 19.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Actually, hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.54,
      "end_seconds": 26.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "I'm, I'm here because of sharp pain when I breathe in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.63,
      "end_seconds": 29.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.96,
      "end_seconds": 41.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "It's a... um, um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.56,
      "end_seconds": 44.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.25,
      "end_seconds": 61.99,
      "duration_seconds": 15.74,
      "text": "uh, for my acidity, I believe my son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given i take allopurinol, 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.71,
      "end_seconds": 68.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.25,
      "end_seconds": 80.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I take Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 81.89,
      "end_seconds": 89.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "it's meant to be twice a day, though I don't see he take it every time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.9,
      "end_seconds": 96.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Yeah, I used to take omeprazole, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.29,
      "end_seconds": 103.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "How long has it been like this? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.59,
      "end_seconds": 109.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "it's, It's been like this since this morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.09,
      "end_seconds": 114.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Alright, how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.49,
      "end_seconds": 126.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "I'd say mild oh, and sudden shortness of breath that's been about the same, about a month"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.78,
      "end_seconds": 133.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Okay, have you been coughing up a little blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.9,
      "end_seconds": 138.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.61,
      "end_seconds": 143.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.02,
      "end_seconds": 151.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.04,
      "end_seconds": 159.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.74,
      "end_seconds": 163.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "I'd say on and off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.91,
      "end_seconds": 168.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "How about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.46,
      "end_seconds": 172.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 178.62,
      "end_seconds": 185.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.22,
      "end_seconds": 194.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "I mean, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.08,
      "end_seconds": 207.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. And what about chest tightness or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.45,
      "end_seconds": 211.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "nope, um, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.77,
      "end_seconds": 215.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.77,
      "end_seconds": 218.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.35,
      "end_seconds": 224.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.48,
      "end_seconds": 230.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Well, yes, grass pollen. I get sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.65,
      "end_seconds": 237.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.95,
      "end_seconds": 241.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.32,
      "end_seconds": 246.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.47,
      "end_seconds": 252.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.1,
      "end_seconds": 255.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.66,
      "end_seconds": 274.16,
      "duration_seconds": 16.5,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid. Yes, acid reflux. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've had gout, yes. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.81,
      "end_seconds": 279.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.55,
      "end_seconds": 281.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.39,
      "end_seconds": 289.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Right, so an underactive thyroid is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.54,
      "end_seconds": 308.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.01,
      "end_seconds": 313.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.98,
      "end_seconds": 318.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.76,
      "end_seconds": 324.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.4,
      "end_seconds": 329.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.6,
      "end_seconds": 339.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Right, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.11,
      "end_seconds": 366.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 90 percent, BP is 131 over 80. And heart rate 95, temp 37.4 degrees, respiratory rate 26."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.69,
      "end_seconds": 394.6,
      "duration_seconds": 20.91,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is a possible blood clot in the lung. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. A A chest infection is also on my list. A D-dimer blood test is what I'd like next, for possible clot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 395.19,
      "end_seconds": 399.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 9 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.97,
      "end_seconds": 407.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "A CT scan of the chest is what I'd like next, for breathlessness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.01,
      "end_seconds": 414.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Okay, so when would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.16,
      "end_seconds": 438.78,
      "duration_seconds": 22.62,
      "text": "You need to go to hospital now for a scan. I think the medical team should see you too. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the the dose. I'll want another look straight away. So, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.35,
      "end_seconds": 444.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.16,
      "end_seconds": 446.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}